[36m(TaskRunner pid=3019342)[0m     "snippet": "---\ntitle: All About Shannen Doherty's Parents, John and Rosa Doherty\nauthor: Skyler Caruso\ndate: 2024-07-15\n---\nShannen Doherty's relationship with her mom and dad was special.\n\nThe late Beverly Hills, 90210 star, who died at age 53 on July 13 after years of living with cancer, is the daughter of Rosa and John Doherty, whom she often talked fondly about through the years.\n\n\"I think I was always a fighter,\" Doherty previously recalled of her childhood, crediting her parents for her tenacity. \"I was raised that way to be very strong and that I could do anything that I put my mind to.\"\n\nDoherty's father, John, died in November 2010 after suffering a stroke on Christmas Day nearly a year prior. In March 2023, the Charmed alum posted a heartfelt Instagram tribute to her late dad on his birthday.\n\n\"I miss him everyday,\" she wrote in part alongside a slideshow of images. \"This year has been one for the books and I desperately wish he was here to help guide me. He always gave me the strength I needed to do what needed to be done.\"\n\nShe continued, \"He stood by my side with love and kindness and that allowed me to go thru hurt and pain with a little less cause he was there. He was the example of what every man should strive to be. A rock. A source of deep love. A guide. Honest. Loyal to his core. Yeah, I miss him. Deeply.\"\n\nDoherty's bond with her mother, Rosa, was just as special. While she admired her mother for her strength and support, she also made her mom's health a \"priority.\"\n\n\"My priority at the moment is my mom,\" Doherty admitted on her Let's Be Clear podcast in April 2024. \"Because it's going to be so hard on her, I want other things to be a lot easier,\" she expressed at the time.\n\nRead on to learn to learn more about Shannen Doherty's parents, Rosa and John Doherty.\n\nShannen said John was 'the greatest man in the world'\n\nJohn and his wife, Rosa, are the parents of two children, Doherty and her older brother Sean. At the time of Doherty's birth, John worked in a Memphis bank"
